# Teferi's Protection: "All permanents you control phase out." A phased-out permanent is treated as though it does not exist
# (CR 702.26b; its example: "Destroy all creatures" does not destroy it). Bot1 answers Bot2's Wrath of God with it: Bot1's lands,
# Moxen, Thraben Inspector, Walking Ballista and Clue token phase out, and so does Bot1's Rancor, which enchants Bot2's
# Ornithopter - an Aura phases out directly with its controller's permanents, not with what it enchants (CR 702.26g is about
# the permanent it is attached to phasing out). The Wrath destroys only the Ornithopter.
# As Bot1's next untap step begins they phase in (CR 502.1) and untap: the same objects (CR 702.26d) - the token still exists,
# the Ballista keeps its +1/+1 counter, the Inspector makes no second Clue (no "enters" trigger) and nothing of Bot1's left the
# battlefield. Rancor phases in unattached, since what it enchanted is gone (CR 702.26i), and the state-based actions put it into
# the graveyard (CR 704.5m), from which its own ability returns it to Bot1's hand.

